Changelog: 25-11-2026 23:22:09

Added. Publish sends the article to the website (owner, 25-11-2026). Its caption counts the files that differ from
the website's folder, a checkout of the repository GitHub Pages serves, or says Up to date. Its first click
asks for that folder. Then it asks first, writes the article there, removes the pictures it no
longer has, commits only the article's files as "see the changelog" and pushes. It is off while the website is up to
date. A globe beside the info symbol opens the website, at its CNAME or GitHub Pages' address. Preview writes one file with the style sheet, fonts and pictures inside, so a browser in a Flatpak shows it
whole. The quickfix card names four quickfixes and then "and more...", and an And more section shows the small
touches of the portal and the apps.

Changelog: 25-11-2026 21:10:01

Added. Nexus Marketing for BC-250, a development app (owner, 25-11-2026). It writes an article that presents the
portal and every app in it, as a web page in the suite's Bazzite design. The apps, their categories and their marks
come from portal/apps.toml. The words come from nexus_marketing/copy.md, a line per category and per app, and the
tests fail when one is missing. The license and the disclaimer come from the suite's README. The development apps
are left out. The page links to the latest release, the wiki, the Portal Tour and GitHub. It shows stills of the
portal from tools/portal_shots.py, one per category and one of the Settings page. The hero's background is a drawn
placeholder until images/hero.webp is there. Preview opens the page in the browser as one file, with its style
sheet, fonts and pictures inside. A browser in a Flatpak gets only the file it opens. Export writes the page to a
new folder, Screenshots takes the stills again and Text check checks copy.md.
